# Workers uploads everything under the assets directory, which here is the
# repository root. This keeps development files out of the deployed site.
#
# Same job the Jekyll `exclude:` list does in _config.yml, and the two are kept
# in step by hand, because both hosts are live at once and drifting apart would
# quietly re-expose something.
#
# NOTHING ENFORCES THAT. This block used to claim `pages.test.js` held the two
# lists together and that `version.test.js` checked the precache list against
# both; neither is true - there is no pages.test.js, and version.test.js reads
# neither file. It checks the version format, pins the cache name to
# package.json, and rejects redirecting aliases in the precache list, and that
# is all. Corrected rather than left standing, because a comment promising a
# guard that does not exist is worse than no comment.
#
# So the two rules below are discipline, not tests:
#   - nothing the app loads at runtime may appear in either list
#   - anything added to one list belongs in the other
#
# TWO WRANGLER CONFIGS NOW LIVE HERE: wrangler.jsonc at the root for the static
# site, and worker/wrangler.toml for the distribution Worker. A bare
# `wrangler deploy` run from worker/ picked up the ROOT config, deployed the
# site under the Worker's name and left the Worker itself untouched - a very
# quiet way to fail, because it reports success. worker/package.json now passes
# --config on every command: deploy the Worker with
# `npm --prefix worker run deploy`, never a bare wrangler command.

# The Cloudflare Worker: source, schema, config
worker/

# Tests
smoke/
*.test.js
core/Model.test.js
core/questions.test.js

# Build and maintenance tooling
scripts/
tools/
package.json
package-lock.json
node_modules/

# Developer documentation. README and LICENSE stay - the app links to LICENSE.
# fonts/README.md is the one README inside a runtime directory; it ships with
# the fonts rather than being excluded, since excluding it would mean excluding
# fonts/ itself.
DEVELOPING.md

# Config that belongs to the deploy, not to the site
wrangler.jsonc
_config.yml
.assetsignore
.github/

# The design system and the agent tooling. `assets.directory` in wrangler.jsonc
# is the repository root, so anything committed and not listed here is uploaded
# and served - and this folder is ~1.7MB of components, specimen pages and
# documentation that the app itself never loads. Listed whether or not it is
# committed, so committing it later cannot quietly publish it at /.claude/.
.claude/
